  "ai_solution": "1. Start with the equation:\n   2x + 3 = -1/2\n\n2. Subtract 3 from both sides to isolate the term with x:\n   2x + 3 - 3 = -1/2 - 3\n   2x = -1/2 - 3\n\n3. Rewrite 3 as a fraction with denominator 2:\n   3 = 6/2\n   So:\n   2x = -1/2 - 6/2\n\n4. Combine the fractions on the right side:\n   2x = (-1 - 6)/2\n   2x = -7/2\n\n5. Divide both sides by 2 to solve for x:\n   x = (-7/2) \u00f7 2\n\n6. Dividing by 2 is the same as multiplying by 1/2:\n   x = (-7/2) \u00d7 (1/2)\n   x = -7/4\n",
  "ai_final_answer": "x = -7/4",
